== every parameter kind
   Nf	f	f NIL
   P	p	Number 7
   P	p1	String "s t"
   Ntok	tok	tok NIL
   P	p2	Token tok
   P	p3	Var x
   Ng	g	g NIL
   P	p4	MNumber n
   P	p5	MToken t
   O	o	g p4 p5
   Vt	t	t\\ \\
   B	b	t
   B	b5	t x
   T	t5	o b b5
   P	p6	Shape t5
   Nh	h	h NIL
   P	p7	Number 3
   O	o7	h p7
   B	b7	t x x
   T	t7	o7 b7
   P	p8	Operator t7
   P	p9	Quote
   P	p10	MString s
   P	p11	MToken k
   P	p12	MShape sh
   P	p13	MOperator o
   P	p14	MLevel 1 i 0 j 2
   O	o14	f p p1 p2 p3 p6 p8 p9 p4 p10 p11 p12 p13 p14
   T	t14	o14
   read back: f[7:n,
   "s t":s,
   "tok":t,
   x:v,
   "g[NT]{0;1}":sh, (h3:n{2}):op, @, n:n, s:s, k:t, sh:sh, o:op, {'i | 'j''}:l]
   alpha-equal: true
== old formats (read_table + get_term; the last line is the term read)
current: sequent x: a >- a:                  Arg: sa
Hyps:
      1.x :a
Goal:a
<= 1.0.10: hypothesis with no variable:      Arg: sa
Hyps:
      1.a
Goal:a
Warning: converting a term read from an old .prla file
<= 1.0.7: context as v::terms:               Arg: sa
Hyps:
      1.<H[a]>
Goal:a
<= 1.0.6: S args::hyps, then G:              Arg: sa
Hyps:
      1.x :a
Goal:a
<= 1.0.6: G with no S before it:             raised Invalid_argument("ASCII IO: invalid entry encountered by add_goal")
<= 1.0.14: two conclusions (the first kept): Arg: sa
Hyps:
Goal:a
<= 1.0.14: no conclusion, no t4:             raised Invalid_argument("ASCII IO: invalid entry encountered by get_term - empty file")
<= 1.0.14: no conclusion, t4 defined:        Arg: sa
Hyps:
Goal:a
<= 1.0.7: var opname with subterms:          'x[a]
<= 1.0.7: var opname, bound subterm:         raised Invalid_argument("Ascii_io: invalid old-style variable term")
<= 1.0.5: MVar parameter:                    a[x:v]
a parameter kind that does not exist:        raised Invalid_argument("ASCII IO: invalid entry encountered by add_param")
MLevel with an odd variable list:            raised Invalid_argument("ASCII IO: invalid entry encountered by level_exp_vars")
== malformed lines (the term is the last line)
O with no fields:                            raised Invalid_argument("ASCII IO: invalid entry encountered by add_op")
N with three fields:                         raised Invalid_argument("ASCII IO: invalid entry encountered by add_name")
B with no fields:                            raised Invalid_argument("ASCII IO: invalid entry encountered by add_bterm")
H with three fields:                         raised Invalid_argument("ASCII IO: invalid entry encountered by add_hyp")
C with an empty field list:                  raised Invalid_argument("ASCII IO: invalid entry encountered by add_context")
S with four groups:                          raised Invalid_argument("ASCII IO: invalid entry encountered by add_seq")
V with one group:                            raised Invalid_argument("ASCII IO: invalid entry encountered by add_var")
var opname, a Number parameter:              raised Invalid_argument("Term.base_ds.make_term with var_opname, but the term does not look like a variable")
a comment and a blank line:                  a
Ascii_io: syntax error on line 4
a line with one field, then a term z:        a
a name defined twice:                        raised Invalid_argument("ASCII IO: invalid entry encountered by hash_add_new key=t9")
Warning: converting a term read from an old .prla file
== get_named_term on a <= 1.0.7 file: Arg: sa
Hyps:
      1.<H[a]>
Goal:a
